.TH TINYDNS 1 "2026-07-23" "rgbdns 0.6.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tinydns \- authoritative DNS server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tinydns
.SH DESCRIPTION
Loads a compiled tinydns zone database and serves authoritative DNS over UDP
and TCP. By default it writes one original-compatible, untimestamped request
record to standard error for each UDP, TCP, and AXFR query. A supervisor may
send this stream to the system journal or to
.BR multilog (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DATA
Database path (default: data.cdb).
.TP
.B IP, PORT
Listen address and port (defaults: 0.0.0.0 and 53).
.TP
.B QUERY_LOG
Enable per-request logging (default: 1). Values 0, false, no, and off disable
it. Log records use hexadecimal client address, port, request ID, and query
type fields followed by the escaped query name. The result markers are + for
an attempted answer, - for refused authority or AXFR, I for an unimplemented
request, C for an unsupported class, and / for a malformed request. Timestamps
are deliberately omitted so journald or
.B multilog t
can add them.
.TP
.B DNSCACHEIP
Comma-separated recursive resolver addresses used to refresh ANAME targets.
If unset, nameservers are read from
.IR /etc/resolv.conf .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tinydns-data (1),
.BR tinydns-get (1),
.BR tinydns-conf (1),
.BR multilog (1)
